#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The live round's driver (plan.md step 3; inputs#I3 for its pty host).

  live-hold.py rehearse-verify | live-verify        viola verify --record on a fresh home
  live-hold.py rehearse-wrapped | live-wrapped      one wrapped start: readings, refusals, keys, hold, killed wrapper
  live-hold.py rehearse-unwrapped | live-unwrapped  one unwrapped start: the status-line reading, a Ctrl-C stop
  live-hold.py derive-state <base>                  round-state.json read from a kept verify home (no start)
  live-hold.py rehearse-derive                      derive-state's two arms under the fake agent
  live-hold.py stamp-check <base>                   entry 21: the kept stamp read, no start and no write
  live-hold.py rehearse-reuse                       entry 23: a second live-form start on a used fake home
  live-hold.py rehearse-trust-form                  entry 24: the trust step against the measured 2.1.325 form

Each prints ONE closing line `{subcommand}: green|red|unread — {codes}` (exit 0 green, 1 red or unread, 3 refused)
and nothing that holds a path, prompt, assistant text, id or pid. A `live-*` subcommand reads founder-words.md
first and refuses (`refused: word {fork} unanswered`, nothing made or started) on a line it needs; a `rehearse-*`
one reads no founder line and drives the fake agent, both the granted and the refused key arm.

Its sessions run on a pty it opens itself in live-pty.py's form (size, declared environment, the Ctrl-C stop);
it adds only the key writes a founder line grants and an in-memory scan of the drained bytes, of which it keeps
counts alone. Every spawn has a kill deadline. Run from the repository root.
"""
